re the base. It then formed a base for about 10 weeks, peaking at $24.38 and pulling back 26% at its deepest. Daily price ranges stayed about the same width through the base.","outcome":"On Feb 19, 2021 it closed at $24.59, its first close above the base high of $24.38. Volume that day was 52.5M shares, 1.60x the prior 10-day average of 32.8M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $29.79, and the chart ends at $28.56.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}